{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/827402-equipment-in-the-shadow","id":827402,"title":"Equipment in the Shadow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-10T04:21:53-08:00","id":827402,"title":"Equipment in the Shadow","content":"I tried searching to see if this had already been answered but couldn't find where it had been; I know in 2.0 clothing melds automatically depending on the werewolf's harmony but I was wondering if a Reaching werewolf's clothing transitions into the Shadow with them or remains behind as it did in 1.0 without the Rite of Dedication. I couldn't find anywhere it was specifically addressed but curious; if inanimate objects do carry over, for instance, werewolves could bring a shotgun or whatever else with them. It's not a huge deal just wondering if there was anything official or if the devs had some insight. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:44:23-08:00","id":827416,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb goes &quot;Can you wear it?&quot; (For a shotgun, it's yes) if yes, it reaches with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:46:53-08:00","id":827418,"title":"","content":"There is no longer a Rite of Dedication, things go along with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:18:13-08:00","id":830624,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Ephsy. If you can wear it, if you're carrying it, you can take it into the shadow. However, objects larger than your urhan form +1 can't go through (yes I know, basically hishu form lol). I usually like to play fast and easy with rites because they're so easy to make up, so it'd be really simple to come up with a Ritual of Binding of some sort that allows large objects, or perhaps lots of stuff in general, to be transported through the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:59:35-08:00","id":840427,"title":"","content":"It would be more a Rite to <i>send</i> something over.<br /> Seems like a third dot Rite. Prolly Extended over minutes requiring Sux equal to the Size of the object plus the Gauntlet's local Strength. Remember material objects 'pushed' across the Gauntlet become ephemeral in the Shadow, When 'pushed' across back they regain their material quality.<br /> But ephemeral things resident of the Shadow enter a state of Twilight in the Material and must be Manifested to become Material. Or so I understand from 1e Mage where this question might come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}